\0
In 2598, the Imperium developed an experimental atmospheric processing device in order to accelerate the development of habitable ecosystems. When tested, however, the device malfunctioned and caused catastrophic biological devastation on the trial world of Perlen, and the planet was quarantined.\n\n
Over a century later, the Freedom Guard landed on the planet's surface and determined that Perlen's atmosphere had recovered to a state where it could support life. They intended to establish a clandestine base there, believing that the Imperium would continue to ignore the planet. However, the Imperium had similar ideas and had already begun constructing fortifications on Perlen. The Freedom Guard landing party clashed with Imperium forces already on the planet.
\1
Freedom Guard forces on Perlen have met with a nominal Imperium force while attempting to develop a base. They appear to be attempting to re-establish an Imperium presence on the planet. If the Imperium troops can be dispatched quickly, the Imperium may attribute the disappearance to ongoing biological contamination and suspend further investigation.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
--> Establish a base\n
--> Destroy the Imperium Power Generator to the\n
\s\s\s\s north\n
--> Assemble a strike force and demolish the\n
\s\s\s\s Imperium base\n
\2
Your successes are encouraging. Forge ahead.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
The Freedom Guard contingent on Perlen ambushed the Imperium and routed them before the Imperium troops could contact their command ship. Attributing the squad's disappearance to Perlen's atmosphere, the Imperium ceased exploration of the planet. The Freedom Guard was able to establish a base on the planet that remained one of their primary fortifications throughout the conflict.
\3
Your failure is disheartening.

